{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeSemisimpleReal","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeSemisimpleReal","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeSemisimpleGeneral"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.semisimple_of_one_lt_unconditional","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.semisimple_of_one_lt_unconditional","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeSemisimpleReal.lean#L79-L91","doc":"**`semisimple_of_one_lt`, with the criterion discharged (sorry-free).**\n\nThe composition: no cited class remains between `1 < q` and semisimplicity\nat every rank.\n\nScope, so this is not over-read: semisimplicity is a magnitude-axis fact.\nNothing here bears on the `P ≠ NP` wall, and the counting-to-decision\ntransfer is untouched. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.wenzlCriterion_of_one_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.wenzlCriterion_of_one_lt","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeSemisimpleReal.lean#L62-L77","doc":"**A model for the cited `WenzlCriterion` (sorry-free).**\n\nFor any real `q > 1`, the criterion holds with `semisimple n` instantiated\nas actual semisimplicity of the rank-`n` algebra.  This is what the class\nwas asking for and had never been supplied.\n\nThe `WenzlGeneric` hypothesis is not used: over `ℝ`, `1 < q` already gives\nsemisimplicity outright, so the criterion is satisfied a fortiori.  Note\nthat a *blanket* instance quantified over all `q` would be **false** as the\nclass is stated — `WenzlGeneric 0 n` holds vacuously (`0 ^ k = 0 ≠ 1`)\nwhile `q = 0` is degenerate — which is why this is a theorem taking `hq`,\nnot an `instance`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.isSemisimpleRing_hecke_of_one_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.isSemisimpleRing_hecke_of_one_lt","kind":"theorem","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeSemisimpleReal.lean#L37-L52","doc":"**The substrate discharges semisimplicity at every rank (sorry-free).**\n\nFor any real `q > 1` — in particular the substrate `q₀ ≈ 1.10998` —\n`QOU.SchurWeyl.Hecke ℝ q q⁻¹ n` is semisimple at every rank.  This is the\nshape in which the substrate parameter discharges the semisimplicity leg of\nthe `P ≠ NP`-in-QOU counting argument, with no cited class and no `sorry`.\n\nThe carrier is named explicitly rather than called \"the Iwahori–Hecke\nalgebra\", because this file's scope section distinguishes it from\n`QOU.Hecke.IwahoriHecke`, and the informal name would read as a claim about\nthat one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.isSemisimpleRing_hecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.isSemisimpleRing_hecke","kind":"theorem","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeSemisimpleReal.lean#L27-L35","doc":"**The `ℝ` specialisation**, in the hypothesis shape the substrate uses.\n\nOver `ℝ` — and only over `ℝ` — `q ≠ 0` together with `q ^ 2 ≠ 1` already says `q` is not a\nroot of unity, which is what `QOU.SchurWeyl.GenericParameter.ofSqNeOne` supplies.  Over a\ngeneral field that implication fails at a primitive fourth root of unity, so the generic\nstatement above carries the criterion directly. ","signatureChunk":0}]}